<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.56.0 (2026-11-25): The Lineage record now states lineageArchived false, the form the archive tool reads before it archives. 1.55.0 (2026-11-25): Merged register. The 54 delta files 1.1.0 to 1.54.0 are combined into one file holding the latest state of every item, so that BRSF's archive tool, which reads one file, can run. Nothing is added or changed in meaning: the latest state of each item and the formal outcome Out_Achieved (1.54.0) are kept; the free-text outcome of 1.53.0 is not carried over, its text stays in the closure report and in 1.53.0 in the git history."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.56.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.56.0" .

ex:CR11_Chapter11First a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Do chapter 11 before chapter 10"@en ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-24 08:02 Istanbul (content, not a verbatim quotation): he wants chapter 11 urgently." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Backlog11 .

ex:ClosureReport11 a backlog:ClosureReport ;
    rdfs:label "Closure report: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:closesForMission ex:Mission11 ;
    backlog:closureCommittedAt "a00e654425d76e31f72af215b25534af508f2629" ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "Partial achievement. Chapters 10 and 11 carry 37 code examples in one piece each, identical on slide and page. Five of six objectives met (differences 0, split boxes 0, examples run 37, verdicts 24, tools 3). Traced examples are 27 of 37, so that target was missed; ten examples name no book block. The full account is in 07-lineage/CLOSURE_REPORT_sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage_Lineage11_v1_0_0.md." ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-11-25T09:20:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective ex:Obj11_NeutralTools,
        ex:Obj11_PageExamplesRun,
        ex:Obj11_ReviewVerdicts,
        ex:Obj11_SlidePageDiffs,
        ex:Obj11_SplitCodeSlides,
        ex:Obj11_TracedExamples .

ex:IA11_ConceptPanels a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the concept panels hold today, measured before anything is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_ConceptPanels ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Cost named: a new A-box version and a new page version for each of the two chapters, one more story each, and a new page test run each (about 16 minutes). The deck and the source stay unchanged unless a book line needs a program that the source does not hold." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-24, read-only, from page data 9.21.0 of chapter 10 and 9.22.0 of chapter 11): a concept panel is the page card of one concept of the chapter; it holds the explanation, the book's own line for the concept (chapter 10: 39 of 59 panels; chapter 11: 44 of 64) and a Try it run (36 and 42). The Try it runs are not book code: 32 of the 36 in chapter 10 and all 42 in chapter 11 are one-line expressions written for the page with import and temporary-folder tricks, stored in the chapter's domain A-box (hasIOExample) and run by page data 2.29.0. The Lab pane Chapter examples (18 in chapter 10, 19 in chapter 11) still reads the old deck transcript, not the book code. Both are the first objection of 2026-11-20 (code that is not the book's) left standing on the page. REASONS AGAINST that hold: a book line that is only a fragment (an ellipsis, a bare method call, a security warning) cannot run alone, so it runs inside the book program of the chapter source that holds it, or carries a named reason, as the source already does. IMPACT: the A-box of each chapter gets a new version whose Try it inputs are the book's lines with the hidden set-up of the source; the Chapter examples pane is made from the manifest; both pages are rebuilt and tested again. No slide changes." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 .

ex:IA11_ExamResults a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the lock touches today, measured before planning"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_ExamResults ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Open: whether chapters 1 to 9 and 12 to 25 take the new template (one Owner question to follow after the proof on chapters 10 and 11, since standing rule 2026-11-11 holds presented chapters unchanged until the book is finished). Decided as a default, without asking: student number, name and surname become optional and are used only in the downloadable result file. The instructor desk still issues release codes that the page no longer asks for; not changed here." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-24, read-only): in page template 9.53.7 the mock exam is one tab (Practice, Mock exam) that holds the start controls, the questions, the marked report and the list of earlier attempts. Template 9.19.0 added a graded layer on top: the exam cannot start without student number, name and surname; after Finish only a Submitted notice shows; the score and the correction under each question open only with an instructor release code checked against the instructor's public key. The template has 11 references to the release lock and the page test 9.40.0 has 10 lines that depend on it. The review of an earlier attempt, the retake of the same code and the list of attempts already exist in the base template; the lock hides the result from them too. The instructor's result desk (2.2.0) re-marks the result files and compares the page's own total in them (page_total), so that field stays in the result file. The chapter pages of every chapter carry the same tab through the shared template. Scope of this lineage is chapters 10 and 11 only; the shared template change is built once and reusable." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 .

ex:IA11_ExamResultsAll a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Which pages can take the change as they are, measured before planning"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_ExamResultsAll ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Excluded and stated: chapters 21 to 25 take the template when they are built to the standard. Open: the instructor's result desk still issues release codes that no page asks for." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-25, read-only, the template patch tried on a copy of each latest page): chapters 1 to 9 and 12 to 20 (18 pages, templates 9.52.2 to 9.53.5) accept the patch unchanged. Chapters 21 to 25 (5 pages, page 9.35.0, templates 9.49.0 and 9.50.0) do not: their file header differs, they are not at the page standard of the others and are unfinished chapters. Rebuilding the 18 from data would also pull in every other template change since their last build, so the change is applied to the existing page instead: one retrofit step per page keeps all other content and only replaces the exam parts, the version marks and the versioned data copies. Each of the 18 pages needs a new version (a relaxation, so a minor step), a test run and a log." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 .

ex:IA11_NoAnalogies a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Where the analogies are today, measured before planning"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_NoAnalogies ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Excluded and stated: chapters 1 to 9 and 12 to 25. Decision made by me, not asked: the analogy slides become plain slides that say what each concept does in a program, in literal words, with no comparison to another thing." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-25, read-only): chapter 10 deck has 7 analogy slides titled Everyday pictures, holding 52 concept lines, and chapter 11 deck has 5 such slides with 23 concept lines; each deck also carries two fixed analogy sentences (a packing list for the summary, finger scales for the practice slide) that the shared deck builder of other chapters carries too. The lecture tab of the chapter 11 page repeats the five slides' text; the speaker notes of the analogy slides use the same pictures (notes 4.0.0: 4 phrase hits in chapter 10, 2 in chapter 11; the later notes files have none in these phrases); chapter 10's code source has 1 phrase hit that grooming must read. Replacing the content on the same slides keeps the slide count at 41 in both decks. The two decks' page tests, deck checks and the code check must be re-run, and the previous versions stay. Other chapters carry the same builder sentences and the same kind of slides; they are out of this lineage." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 .

ex:IA11_RepeatsWindows a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What repeats and what is Linux-flavoured today, measured before planning"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_RepeatsWindows ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Open: how Windows is shown (one Owner question to follow). Separate gap noted, not in this change: the ruling against everyday analogies is not yet applied to chapters 10 and 11." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-24, read-only, story repeat check over chapters 1 to 25): chapter 10 has 4 stories, two repeat: the UTF-8 diner story has the same link and the same two names as chapter 8; the JSON story shares both people with chapter 7. The dbm story shares only a person's name with chapters 8 and 9 (different events). Chapter 11 has 4 stories and none repeats. Results: the page already accepts multi-line outputs (test 9.40.0); only the one-line prediction field is limiting. Platform: recorded outputs show Linux path types today. Cost named: replace 2 chapter 10 stories in place (slide count unchanged), new deck, source, page versions and tests for chapter 10; Windows presentation touches both chapters." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 .

ex:IA11_Reuse a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What reuse across chapters and courses needs, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_Reuse ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Cost named: two more areas, a reusable tool set and a method guide; the two chapters stay the only chapters converted." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-20, read-only): the repository holds 43 chapter-code manifests, all with the same example shape (order, id, name, slide, concepts, code, expected; some add recorded), so one shared source format and one generic check can serve every chapter without changing their shape. Chapters 10 and 11 show three faults that any chapter can have: code that is not the book's (7 and 8 percent of lines match), code split over boxes (all 37 code slides), slide and page examples that differ (5 of 37). IMPACT: a generic check and a generic source-to-slide-and-page step are built once inside this lineage and proven on chapters 10 and 11; they carry no chapter-specific text. Other chapters and other courses are NOT converted here; they adopt the method in their own lineages. Course-neutral wording goes in a written method guide in the course meta-model's own place, handed over through that repository's standard handover folder only if the Owner asks." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    rdfs:comment "Correction recorded in 1.4.0: the impact statement gives 5 of 37 slide and page examples that differ and splits on all 37; the measured figures are 7 of 37 and 35 of 37 (chapter 10: slides 10 and 28; chapter 11: slides 7, 14, 22, 27, 28). The impact on scope is unchanged."@en .

