ex:TK11_Check_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Write the generic check for the three conditions"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Make_Verify ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "08-tooling/code_check_v1_0_0.py: four conditions on a chapter source file: C1 examples list equals source in order, C2 each source slide has exactly one code box equal to the source code, C3 the page data holds the whole code string as the source has it, C4 setup plus code runs to the end. No chapter text. Accepts the examples list or the chapter-code manifest wrapper." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ;
    backlog:hasTransitionNote "Starts 2026-11-20 after the Owner's go at 23:35 Istanbul; its dependency TK11_Make_Verify is Done." .

ex:TK11_Check_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Run it on a good toy and on three broken copies, one per condition; read the log"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Check_Build ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0: check_toy_run.log (good toy passes all four; five broken copies, each refused under its own condition and named message), make_1_1_0_toy_run.log (two identical runs, the tab runs), check_old_decks_baseline.log (the existing chapter 10 and 11 decks 3.0.0: C2 fails on 18 of 18 and 19 of 19 code slides, C1 and C3 pass against the manifests 1.1.0 and pages 9.20.0). A first harness run had two wrong results, caused by my test (slide numbers not padded; a page check that accepted a prefix), and by a weak page condition; both fixed and rerun before this record. Run by the agent that wrote the tool, so not independent. Note: the tool counts 37 of 37 failing slides where my hand count said 35 of 37 split; the difference is that C2 also fails a slide whose single box holds extra set-up lines. The objective figure stays as measured by hand and the tool's figure is the one used from now on." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify .

ex:TK11_Code_10_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Trace each subject to the book's blocks; write the source: book programs as they are, shell examples as plain programs with the result as a comment (Owner's option C)"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Check_Verify ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/ch10/source/ch10_code_source_v1_0_0.json: 18 examples in the slide order of deck 3.0.0 (slides 6 to 37, no slide added), 135 code lines, longest line 62 characters, at most 21 lines per example. 15 of 18 are traced to a block or section of the book's chapter 10 in their book field; 3 carry a named reason (modes, encoding, json). The old examples had the temporary folder lines and invented helpers inside the shown code (a fake shelf, an iterator for the Mad Libs answers, a one-line state dictionary); they are replaced by the book's own calls (shelve.open, open with write and append, readlines, the Mad Libs and quiz programs)." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ;
    backlog:hasTransitionNote "Starts 2026-11-24 after the chapter 11 release (register 1.18.0)." .

ex:TK11_Code_10_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Compare each example with its book block from the book file; list every difference and its reason"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Code_10_Build ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Each example compared with its book block read from the book file: 37 of 135 lines (27 percent) are equal to a book line, against 12 of 166 (7 percent) in the old examples; the rest differ for named reasons: the book shows Windows paths and an interactive session, the source prints the result and uses a fixed seed, four states instead of fifty. Log 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0/ch10_source_outputs.log: all 18 run (set-up in one namespace, code in a fresh one) with the same output twice. The two old exceptions are kept: the Windows path example runs on Linux through PureWindowsPath, and the book's sonnet text file is made by the hidden set-up." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify .

ex:TK11_Code_11_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Trace each subject to the book's blocks; write the source with the same rules as chapter 10"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Release_10_Verify ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/ch11/source/ch11_code_source_v1_0_0.json holds the 19 chapter 11 examples once: 10 traced to a block of the book (copy, copytree, move, dry run, listing, walk, mkdir, ZIP write, extract, the finished backup program) and 9 with a named reason in their own book field (the slide teaches it, the book has no code block for it; written in the book's style, 4 to 6 lines). Interpreter prompts removed (Owner's option C), results are print lines. Sample files are hidden setup lines in a temporary folder. Two small changes to keep the same output on every machine: folders and files are sorted in the walk and in the listing. Code lines fell from 285 to 113; 49 percent of them equal a book line, against 7 percent before." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ;
    backlog:hasTransitionNote "Starts 2026-11-24 by CR11_Chapter11First, ahead of its recorded dependency on the chapter 10 release task." .

ex:TK11_Code_11_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ;
    rdfs:label "Compare each example with its book block from the book file; list every difference and its reason"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK11_Code_11_Build ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Log 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0/ch11_source_outputs.log: each of the 19 examples runs to the end and gives the same output twice; the backup program prints exactly the four lines the book shows (Creating spam_1.zip, Adding files in folder spam, Adding file file1.txt, Done); the ZIP example gives the book's sizes 50000 and 97. Code check C1 and C4 pass on the source and its examples list. Run by the agent that wrote the examples, so not independent. Open and named: the deck and page conditions (C2, C3) belong to the next stories; the Owner's reading of the examples is the criterion that no tool can run. Results show PosixPath where the book shows WindowsPath, as the machine here is not Windows." ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify .

