ex:Mission11 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 10 and 11 teach the book's own code, in one piece, run on the page"@en ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's urgency case of 2026-11-20 17:37 Istanbul (objections on slides and code examples of chapters 10 and 11, and the request to review them and plan their simplification)." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_Achieved ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "The SEN0414 chapter 10 and chapter 11 slides and interactive pages are simplified so that every code example is the book's own code for the subject taught, shown in one readable piece that can be copied in one step, identical on the slide and on the page, with the page as the place that shows, explains and runs each code as the slides progress; a teacher can give the session without leaving the page." ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog11 ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "All 19 stories and 39 tasks Done; five of six objectives met (differences 0, split boxes 0, examples run 37, verdicts 24, tools 3); traced examples 27 of 37, target missed. Not shown: the three-role review was made by the building agent and was given before the later changes; the 18 retrofitted pages have only the focused exam results test; the cause of the traced count moving from 25 to 27 was not traced. Details in the closure report." .

ex:Scope11 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 10 and 11: the book's own code, one source, slide and page identical"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area11_Code,
        ex:Area11_Concepts,
        ex:Area11_Deck,
        ex:Area11_ExamResults,
        ex:Area11_NoAnalogies,
        ex:Area11_Page,
        ex:Area11_Release,
        ex:Area11_Repeats,
        ex:Area11_Reuse,
        ex:Area11_Source ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del11_Check,
        ex:Del11_Code_10,
        ex:Del11_Code_11,
        ex:Del11_Concepts_10,
        ex:Del11_Concepts_11,
        ex:Del11_Deck_10,
        ex:Del11_Deck_11,
        ex:Del11_ExamResults,
        ex:Del11_ExamResultsAll,
        ex:Del11_Guide,
        ex:Del11_Make,
        ex:Del11_NoAnalogies,
        ex:Del11_Page_10,
        ex:Del11_Page_11,
        ex:Del11_Release_10,
        ex:Del11_Release_11,
        ex:Del11_Repeats_10,
        ex:Del11_Source_10,
        ex:Del11_Source_11,
        ex:Del11_Windows ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl11_Chapters,
        ex:Excl11_Content,
        ex:Excl11_OtherChapterConversion,
        ex:Excl11_SlideCount ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: chapters 10 (Reading and Writing Files) and 11 (Organizing Files). (a) Code: every example comes from the book's own code for the subject taught, short, one program, no extras; the book's interactive-shell examples become plain programs with the result as a comment, no prompts; test set-up moves out of the visible code into a hidden page step. (b) Source: one source file per chapter holds each example once; the slide, the page example and the Slide code tab are generated from it, so they cannot differ. (c) Deck: each code sits whole in one box, copyable in one step; explanations sit beside or below it, not between code chunks; results show as the real output. (d) Page: every example of the deck runs on the page in slide order, with its explanation, so a session needs no other tool. (e) Release: automatic checks (code equals source on slide and page, one box per code, every example runs) and recorded reviews on teachability, understandability, explainability and human communication."@en ;
    backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission11 .

ex:DoD11 a backlog:DefinitionOfDone ;
